  {
    "episode_id": 79349,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/9/79349.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "You know, I deal, well, often with folks that tend to use this weapon. And when you're dealing with these kind of folks, you know, whether it's online, and I know exactly what you're talking about, I've had some comments made online about me and my work, and yeah, the names are never real, and the comments are pretty mean, and it's easy to be able to do that under the guise of not really showing who you are. And you know, and I can understand where that comes from, but one of the biggest insults I think is when you're dealing with that socially, I live in a building that several people live in, and there's a couple of people that are just constantly passive aggressive. And where does that really come from? Is this that internal anger, or where is that festering from?",
