  {
    "episode_id": 79349,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/9/79349.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "Well, there could be those parts. They could be not respecting you. They could also have no clue what to do. And they're trying to put the argument on their grounds. And the very fact that you just said you felt uncomfortable means you're playing in their court, their basketball court, by their rules, that a functional relationship works from it. Be upfront, be honest, deal with the honesty, even if it hurts. That takes some work, but in a passive aggressive way, you're not going to be direct. You're going to be covert. You're going to be hidden in your anger and you can do some things to undermine that other person, set them off and then you're not on your game. And so they will have an upper hand in those arguments or whatever game they're playing.",
